From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: UBOX10 Research <noreply@example.invalid>
Date: Fri, 21 Aug 2026 15:00:00 +0000
Subject: [PATCH] sepolicy: defer fuseblk root label to API 31 vendor

The accepted UBOX API-31 vendor policy owns the fuseblk root genfscon and
labels it vfat. Android 16's platform rule labels the identical filesystem and
path fuseblk, so secilc rejects the split policy before init can load it.

Remove the platform duplicate for this exact-board prototype. The retained
vendor rule then supplies the same label used by the device-accepted Android
12 baseline. This is a Prototype A compatibility patch, not a platform-wide
policy recommendation.
---
 private/genfs_contexts | 1 -
 1 file changed, 1 deletion(-)

diff --git a/private/genfs_contexts b/private/genfs_contexts
--- a/private/genfs_contexts
+++ b/private/genfs_contexts
@@ -335,7 +335,6 @@
 genfscon exfat / u:object_r:exfat:s0
 genfscon debugfs / u:object_r:debugfs:s0
 genfscon fuse / u:object_r:fuse:s0
-genfscon fuseblk / u:object_r:fuseblk:s0
 genfscon configfs / u:object_r:configfs:s0
 genfscon sdcardfs / u:object_r:sdcardfs:s0
 genfscon esdfs / u:object_r:sdcardfs:s0
